From 6336e40a7d50f1ade0f3dd82557352199881595a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 21:41:41 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 272/638] v8: prove direct AROS shared-library import

Add a focused Chromium-built consumer that calls v8::V8::GetVersion through an AROS runtime import trampoline. Keep the consumer on V8 headers plus v8.library only, and allow the existing focused extraction graph to include explicit consumer gates.

AI_PHASE: v8-library-convergence
AI_STATUS: implemented
AI_ROOT_CAUSE: Chromium calls the V8 C++ ABI directly, while the AROS v8 link library exposes only its small wrapper API; loading v8.library alone would not remove static V8 objects from Chrome.
AI_FIX: Add the first ABI-preserving x86-64 import trampoline and a direct C++ consumer probe resolved by V8FindEngineSymbol; allow root_extra_deps in the focused AROS V8 graph.
AI_VALIDATION: focused GN generation and probe link passed; hosted 16 GiB run resolved _ZN2v82V810GetVersionEv from v8.library, returned 12.4.254, printed direct C++ import PASS, and bootstrap exited 0.
AI_FAILURE: Full strip removed AROS relocations and trapped at RIP=0; preserved as evidence, then corrected with strip --strip-unneeded.
AI_RISK: This proves one function import only; full Chrome requires generated cached trampolines plus classification of direct V8 data symbols.
AI_CHAIN:
